{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## The gap\n\nS1 (`aa40`, change 2620) put the unreachable-scratch **refusal** in `gate_admission()`, which wraps\nplan-review and completion-verifier. That is where ADR 0112 places it, and S1 implements the ADR\nfaithfully.\n\nBut the review-bot's per-review clone does **not** pass through `gate_admission()`. It is a plain\n`tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix=\"reviewbot-\")` in `voter._decision_for_review_target`, following\n`TMPDIR`. So on a **declared-but-unmounted** scratch volume, plan-review and completion-verifier\ncorrectly refuse while the review-bot keeps cloning onto the root filesystem, silently — precisely\nthe outage epic `6202` exists to prevent. A partial refusal is arguably worse than none, because the\nloud half creates confidence the protection is in force.\n\nThis is a gap in the architecture, not a defect in S1.\n\n## The trap (read change 2620 first)\n\nAn unmounted volume raises **nothing**: a mount point whose volume is absent is an ordinary,\nwritable, empty directory, so a naive `mkdir(parents=True)` silently recreates state on root and\nevery caller keeps working. S1's answer is two markers on two different filesystems —\n`.gate-scratch-required` on **root** beside the mount point (the declaration, survives an unmount)\nand `.gate-scratch-mounted` **on the volume** (the proof, vanishes with it). Only\ndeclaration-present + proof-absent refuses.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **Share S1's check, do not reimplement it.** Promote the two-marker predicate inside\n   `gate_admission._require_scratch_volume` to a public `scratch_unavailable_detail()` on\n   `src/rebar/llm/gate_admission.py` (that module is not in the pinned API-surface baseline, so this\n   is not a public-surface change). `_require_scratch_volume` becomes a thin caller that raises\n   `GateScratchUnavailableError`; the review-bot calls the same function. One predicate, one pair of\n   marker constants, so enforcement and `observability.sh` monitoring cannot disagree.\n2. **Guard the clone at the existing pre-clone admission seam.** `_decision_for_review_target`\n   already refuses before cloning when the free-space floor is not met\n   (`if not _review_clone_has_room(cfg): return _low_disk_decision(), \"\"`). Add the scratch check\n   immediately **before** that, and before the `TemporaryDirectory`, so nothing is created on root.\n   Ordering matters: on an unmounted volume the empty mount point usually **passes** the free-space\n   floor, so the scratch check must run first.\n3. **Reuse ADR 0069's existing deferral; invent nothing.** The refusal is returned as an\n   adapter-shaped decision carrying the **existing** `low-disk` retryable gap reason, built by a new\n   `low_disk.scratch_unavailable_decision()` sibling of `low_disk.decision()`. That reason is already\n   in `adapter.RETRYABLE_GAP_REASONS`, so under budget the voter defers vote-less\n   (`REVIEW_RETRY_DEFERRED`), and it is already the **one** reason ADR 0069 carves out to a terminal\n   no-vote on exhaustion (`REVIEW_LOW_DISK_DEFERRED_EXHAUSTED`, labels unchanged) rather than the\n   fail-closed `-1`. A new gap reason would have to be added to that carve-out branch by hand and\n   could regress into a false `LLM-Review -1` on a host condition; reusing the reason makes\n   \"never -1\" structural. The distinct sub-condition is carried in the coverage block\n   (`scratch_unavailable`, `scratch_path`) and in the operator-facing message, not in routing.\n\nOut of scope: `infra/scripts/*` and `infra/terraform/*` (owned by story `9183`, in flight).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 — With the declaration present on the root-side parent and the proof absent from the mount\n      point, the review-bot clone path **refuses**: `review_and_vote` returns a coverage-gap result\n      and `clone_change_ref` is never called. Proven with the real two-marker files on a temp\n      \"host\", not by monkeypatching the predicate.\n- [ ] AC2 — The refusal is an ADR 0069 **retryable deferral**, never an `LLM-Review -1`: under\n      budget the result is `status=\"deferred\"` with no vote posted; with the budget exhausted the\n      result is `status=\"deferred-exhausted\"` with no vote posted, no `VOTER_ERROR`, and labels\n      unchanged.\n- [ ] AC3 — **Absence assertion (defect-seeded).** With declaration present and proof absent, the\n      clone path creates **nothing** on the underlying (root) directory: no `reviewbot-*` entry\n      exists under it after the call. Modelled on S1's\n      `test_the_refusal_creates_no_store_on_the_underlying_directory` — asserts the directory does\n      not exist, not merely that an error was raised. RED first: with the guard removed the same\n      test shows the clone landing there.\n- [ ] AC4 — **No-op preserved.** With no declaration present (the default, and every developer\n      machine and CI runner), nothing changes: the clone proceeds and no refusal occurs. Also\n      asserted for the proof-present/declaration-absent quadrant.\n- [ ] AC5 — Monitoring and enforcement read the **same** proof marker: the review-bot path resolves\n      its markers from `gate_admission`'s own constants via the shared predicate (asserted by\n      identity, not by string duplication), and `observability.sh` continues to name that same\n      marker.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_review_bot.py -k scratch -q` — AC1-AC5 on\n  the review-bot clone path (refusal, absence-on-root, deferred / deferred-exhausted vote-lessness,\n  both no-op quadrants, shared-predicate identity).\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py -q` — S1's\n  suite still passes unchanged, proving the extraction is behaviour-preserving for the gates.\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_review_bot.py tests/unit/test_gate_admission_09da.py -q` — no regression in the low-disk and admission paths that share the seam.\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py tests/unit/test_api_surface_gate.py -q` — the three gates invisible to `make lint` (run after `git add`).\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` and `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`.\n\n## File impact\n\n`src/rebar/llm/gate_admission.py`, `src/rebar/review_bot/low_disk.py`,\n`src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py`, `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py`,\n`tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788533329869797001,"uuid":"96cca622-d163-4f23-b488-45285eb4b13a"}